note
note src/turing/ty_qrecord.om -- Pure seeded OM-2 implementation of TURING
note continuous-value companion records (qprofile, qworld, qfreeze, qgain)
note and sidecar manifest builders/parsers/validators.
note Composed after src/turing/ty_core_lib.om.
note
note Replaces src/turing/ty_qrecord.{c,h}. Same digests (SHA-256(domain || 0x00
note || OMG0 bytes), ca_finish of ty_core_lib), same refusal rules and return
note codes (TY_OK, TY_E_FORMAT, TY_E_DIGEST, TY_E_PROFILE, TY_E_IO, TY_E_ARG,
note TYQR_E_EXISTS). Differences of form, not of result:
note   - each record kind lives in one global record (g_qp_*, g_qw_*, g_qf_*,
note     g_qg_*); string fields are TYQR_VAL-byte NUL-terminated cells, so a
note     513-byte value without NUL is refused exactly as in C;
note   - digests are g_dig slots; slots 500 and 501 are scratch for this file,
note     so callers must not pass them to tyqr_gain_bind or the verifiers;
note   - the free-text refusal reason (C `why`) is not produced; the code is;
note   - NULL-argument TY_E_ARG cases have no counterpart (no pointers);
note   - sidecar build/parse work in g_qr_mbuf (8192 bytes, so at most 8191
note     bytes of output), at most 64 entries (building more is TY_E_ARG,
note     parsing more is TY_E_FORMAT); the written
note     path is left in g_qr_wpath / g_qr_wplen.

const TYQR_VAL ulong 513
const TYQR_MAX_LINEAGE ulong 8
const TYQR_CANON_CAP ulong 40000
const TYQR_CELL_MAX ulong 128
const TYQR_SCRATCH_SLOT ulong 500
const TYQR_VERIFY_SLOT ulong 501

